  "title": "Erdős Problem #940",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Let $r\\geq 3$. A number $n$ is $r$-powerful if for every prime $p$ which divides $n$ we have $p^r\\mid n$.\nAre there infinitely many integers which are not the sum of at most $r$ many $r$-powerful numbers? Does the set of integers which are the sum of at most $r$ $r$-powerful numbers have density $0$?",
